    "report": "The archive feature is finished and committed as `d7cf91d` on `main`, the branch you asked for. Nothing is pushed.\n\n**What the previous developer left, and what I added**\n\nTheir WIP commit had the domain rule, the command handler, and persistence, but no route, no wiring, and no list or unread changes. I kept their work and added the rest:\n\n- **Route:** `POST /conversations/:id/archive`, answered with `acceptCommand` (202 with an operation id), the same as mark-read, per ADR 53.\n- **Wiring:** the archive handler is registered in the Messaging module. Without this the route would have had no handler.\n- **List:** `GET /conversations/mine` leaves out conversations the caller archived, until a newer message is written. The archived flag is computed in the summaries query by comparing the caller's archive with the conversation's last message.\n- **Unread:** `GET /conversations/unread` still counts archived conversations, since it sums every summary line.\n- **Refusals:** a stranger, an unknown id, and an anonymous caller are refused as the spec says. The transport gives the anonymous 401; the handler gives NotFound.\n- **Tests:** three e2e cases in `conversations.routes.e2e.spec.ts` for the archiver-only list, the comeback on a new message from either side, viewer archiving, and the refusals.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- `yarn typecheck` passes. It caught a type error that Jest did not, because ts-jest doesn't type-check here.\n- ESLint and Prettier pass on the Messaging tree.\n- All 69 Messaging tests pass across 13 suites, against the local Postgres. I didn't run the rest of the repo's suite.\n- I didn't start a server, so port 4471 is unused.\n\n**Choices I made where the request was open**\n\n- A message counts as \"written\" even if an upheld report later hides it, because the domain already treats the last message that way.\n- Archiving again rewrites the same archive row and bumps the conversation version, as mark-read already does. What a client sees doesn't change.\n- I didn't update `conventions/storms/conversations.yaml`. It doesn't list every command, so I left it alone.",
